course: dictionary
lesson: 13366
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word «hash» is one of them. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning to use.
explain: «Press hash on the phone to make the # sign.» Here hash is a symbol. «We had hash browns for breakfast.» Here hash is food. The clue is the other words in each sentence.
explain: «She made a hash of her spelling test.» Here hash does not mean food or a symbol. Made a hash of means did it very badly. Always check: does my meaning fit in the sentence?
fact: The # symbol is called a hash sign, a number sign, or a pound sign in the US.
fact: «Hash browns» are fried grated potato, a breakfast food.
fact: «Make a hash of something» means do it very badly.
fact: «Hash out» means to discuss something until you agree.
fact: In computing, a hash is a code made from data by a fixed rule, used to check files and passwords.
exercise: «Press hash on the phone to make the # sign.» What does hash mean here? | To mess something up | A dish of meat and potatoes | *The # symbol | To talk something over
exercise: «He made a hash of his spelling test.» What does made a hash of mean? | Wrote it in code | Ate it for lunch | Did it very well | *Did it very badly
exercise: «We had hash browns for breakfast.» What are hash browns? | Chopped phone numbers | A computer password | *Fried grated potato | A type of drawing
test: «The team had to hash out a plan before they could start.» What does hash out mean? | Press the # key | Cook the plan in a pan | Throw the plan away | *Discuss it until they agree
test: «#summer is a popular hashtag.» Why is the # used? | *To label a post so people can find it | To pay for an app | To tell the time | To make the post louder
exam: «The computer turned the password into a hash, a scrambled code.» What is a hash here? | A tasty breakfast dish | A type of phone | *A code made from data by a fixed rule | A kind of cooking pan
